    {
      "id": 33393,
      "nameEs": "Devil Kings",
      "originalName": "Devil Kings",
      "year": 2005,
      "igdbId": 22568,
      "popularity": 6,
      "iconic": false,
      "fields": [
        {
          "field": "name_es",
          "value": "Devil Kings",
          "source": "igdb",
          "manual": false
        },
        {
          "field": "original_name",
          "value": "Devil Kings",
          "source": "igdb",
          "manual": false
        },
        {
          "field": "summary",
          "value": "Devil Kings is in the same vein as the Dynasty Warriors series. Whereas in Dynasty Warriors, however, Koei focuses on ancient Chinese history, Devil Kings focuses more on feudal Japan, but with a fictional setting with the ability to use modern day weapons such as chain guns and shotguns as well as fighting legendary and fictional characters from the past.\n\nThe story takes place as the Devil King, a king possessed by the soul of the Devil, has unleashed an unholy army on the world to bend it to his will as the player must stop him along with many of his minions including his wife Lady Butterfly, his general the Red Minotaur, as well as loyal assassins Scorpio and Venus.\n\nThe gameplay is more arcade hack-and-slash style, with the ability of using magic spells to wipe out entire waves of enemies and as mentioned before, the ability to use modern day weapons along with historical weapons such as spears, swords among others. There are six playable characters to use as well, each with their own story told in CG and anime cutscenes as well as two modes of play, Conquest (the main story of the game) and Free Mode (where players can play in any unlocked stage they have completed).",
          "source": "igdb",
          "manual": false
        },
        {
          "field": "summary_es",
          "value": "Devil Kings sigue la misma línea que la serie Dynasty Warriors. Sin embargo, mientras que Dynasty Warriors se centra en la historia antigua de China, Koei se centra en Devil Kings en el Japón feudal, pero con un escenario ficticio que permite usar armas modernas como ametralladoras y escopetas, además de luchar contra personajes legendarios y ficticios del pasado.\n\nLa historia transcurre cuando el Rey Demonio, un rey poseído por el alma del Diablo, ha desatado un ejército infernal sobre el mundo para someterlo a su voluntad. El jugador debe detenerlo, junto con muchos de sus secuaces, entre ellos su esposa Lady Butterfly, su general el Minotauro Rojo, y los leales asesinos Scorpio y Venus.\n\nLa jugabilidad es más de estilo arcade, de hack and slash, con la posibilidad de usar hechizos mágicos para aniquilar oleadas enteras de enemigos y, como se mencionó antes, de utilizar armas modernas junto con armas históricas como lanzas, espadas, entre otras. Hay seis personajes jugables, cada uno con su propia historia contada en escenas CG y de anime, así como dos modos de juego: Conquista (la historia principal del juego) y Modo libre (donde los jugadores pueden jugar en cualquier escenario desbloqueado que hayan completado).",
          "source": "claude",
          "manual": false
        },
        {
          "field": "year",
          "value": "2005",
          "source": "igdb",
          "manual": false
        }
      ],
